<h2 id="chronoforge-experience-as-experimental-infrastructure">12. ChronoForge: Experience as Experimental Infrastructure</h2>
<div class="wp-callout"><strong>CHRONOFORGE THESIS  </strong>Do not give an artificial system six months of data. Give it six months of life - then compare what the experience changed.</div>
<p>ChronoForge is the planned LUNA subsystem for controlled developmental time. It is designed to create coherent simulated timelines in which actions have consequences, people and projects recur, feedback can arrive later, ordinary repetition establishes a baseline, and the running participant can be changed by what happens.</p>
<p>The distinction from synthetic training data is causal. If a simulator merely writes both sides of a transcript and injects it into memory, it has produced data. In a ChronoForge experience, the participant perceives a situation, chooses an action, encounters a world consequence, carries the result forward, and later meets situations whose meaning depends on that history.</p>

